@startuml domain_class_diagram
title Medical Tracker — Domain Class Diagram (docs/domain_model.md)

hide circle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class User {
  +id : Identifier
  +email : string <<unique, case-insensitive>>
  +password : hashed credential
  +timezone : IANA timezone id
}

class ExaminationCategory {
  +id : Identifier
  +name : string <<unique>>
  +slug : string <<unique>>
}
note right of ExaminationCategory
  Fixed, seeded via idempotent migration,
  read-only for MVP users. A null category
  on ExaminationRecord is presented as
  "Uncategorized" — not a stored row.
end note

class ExaminationRecord {
  +id : Identifier
  +title : string
  +medical_specialty : string [0..1]
  +scheduled_date : date [0..1]
  +scheduled_time : time [0..1]
  +completed_date : date [0..1]
  +status : {draft, planned, completed, cancelled, missed}
  +location : string [0..1]
  +notes : text [0..1]
  +created_at : datetime <<tz-aware>>
  +updated_at : datetime <<tz-aware>>
}
note right of ExaminationRecord
  Status-dependent required fields:
  - draft: title only
  - planned / cancelled / missed: + scheduled_date
  - completed: + completed_date (<= today)
  Every create/update validates the complete
  resulting record, not just the submitted diff.
  "overdue" is derived at query time — never
  a stored value (see domain_model.md §7).
end note

class Reminder {
  +id : Identifier
  +offset_days : positive integer
  +due_date : date [0..1] <<derived: scheduled_date - offset_days>>
  +is_active : boolean
  +created_at : datetime <<tz-aware>>
  +updated_at : datetime <<tz-aware>>
}
note right of Reminder
  May be active only while its examination is
  planned. Leaving planned deactivates it (not
  deleted); returning to planned does not
  auto-reactivate it. Persists across every
  status change.
end note

class RecurrenceRule {
  +id : Identifier
  +interval : {monthly, six_months, yearly}
  +created_at : datetime <<tz-aware>>
  +updated_at : datetime <<tz-aware>>
}
note right of RecurrenceRule
  Create/modify only while planned. The rule
  itself persists unchanged across every status
  change. Next-occurrence creation is idempotent
  per (source, calculated due date).
end note

User "1" -- "*" ExaminationRecord : owns >
ExaminationCategory "0..1" -- "*" ExaminationRecord : classifies >
ExaminationRecord "1" -- "0..1" Reminder : has >
ExaminationRecord "1" -- "0..1" RecurrenceRule : has >
ExaminationRecord "0..1" -- "*" ExaminationRecord : source_occurrence\n(generates) >

note as DeleteNote
  Deleting an examination cascades to its
  Reminder and RecurrenceRule. Deleting an
  examination referenced by another's
  source_occurrence sets that reference to
  null instead of deleting or blocking it.
end note

@enduml
